In other words, this machine cannot run experiments on TorchOpt. The task itself is design-only anyway ("Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.", "Do not claim that an experiment was run").

APIs from prior knowledge (must be explicitly noted as unverified): TorchOpt's `torchopt.diff` module. The TorchOpt paper (arXiv 2409.19569, "TorchOpt: A High-Performance PyTorch Compiler-Compatible Optimizer Library"? Actually "TorchOpt: An Efficient High-Performance and Compiler-Assisted Optimizer Library for Meta-Learning on JAX/PyTorch") describes an "explicit gradient" mechanism for differentiable operations of optimizers: instead of relying on autograd through iterative loops (e.g., implicit differentiation via unrolled fixed-point iterations), it registers custom gradients that reuse forward-pass intermediate results. In the TorchOpt source, related files include:
